                                                "example_id": "8f6ba35a-f32c-457e-b482-fe20b2e87515",
                                                "sense_id": "ee208c97-4ac0-3fbc-865a-aae0526f684d",
                                                "text": "Geographie is (according to Ptolomei) an imitation of the picture of the vvhole Earth. […] VVe take not the Earth ſimply in its ovvn nature as it is an element, for ſo it belongeth to Philoſophy, but for the terreſtrial Globe, ſo it is the ſubiect of Geographie, and is defined to bee a Sphericall body, proportionably compoſed of earth, and vvater."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5035e7e8-1349-30ff-94db-ffd39e93aeb0",
                                        "entry_id": "ca220a5b-2d77-3da0-abba-bea1ee64364c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Terrain: the physical properties of a region of the earth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "55314000-1e15-42e9-a965-d20301d22499",
                                                "sense_id": "5035e7e8-1349-30ff-94db-ffd39e93aeb0",
                                                "text": "The geography of the Andes approaches never made transportation easy; routes to Bogota, Quito, La Paz, and Cuzco were so precipitous as to slow down the development of those Spanish cities in the interior."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
